alpha_1h_0)\mathrm{e}^{-(\alpha _1 - \alpha_2) w}h_{d,w,	heta_2,1}<0,\qquad 0<w\le1 . \] Note that $\psi(0+)=(\alpha_1 - \alpha_2) h_0^2<0$ and thus $\psi(w)<0$ for all $0<w\le1$. Since reak $\mathrm{e}^{\alpha_2w }h_{d,w,	heta_1,1}^2  rac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}w}H_{	heta_1,	heta_2}(w)=\psi(w)<0$ for all $0 < w \le 1$, $H_{	heta_1,	heta_2}$ is strictly decreasing with $H_{	heta_1,	heta_2}(0+)=1$, contradicting (ef{centralidentitynoneq2}). This completes the proof of (v).

